What is Mockito?

Mockito is a popular Java testing framework used to create mock objects for unit testing. It helps test a class without depending on real implementations of external classes or APIs.

Advantages
Creates fake (mock) objects.
Isolates the class under test.
Makes unit testing faster.
Reduces dependency on databases, APIs, or external services.
Verifies method interactions.
Important Mockito Methods
Method	Purpose
mock()	Creates a mock object.
when()	Defines mock behavior (stubbing).
thenReturn()	Specifies the value returned by a mock method.
verify()	Checks whether a method was called.
times()	Verifies how many times a method was invoked.
assertEquals()	Compares expected and actual values.
Example Structure
External API (Dependency)
          │
          ▼
      Mock Object
          │
          ▼
     MyService Class
          │
          ▼
      Unit Test
1. External API Interface

The ExternalApi interface represents an external dependency used by the service.

interface ExternalApi {

    String getData();

    String getDataById(int id);

}
Purpose
Represents an external API.
Will be replaced with a mock during testing.
Avoids calling a real service.
2. Service Class (Class Under Test)

The MyService class depends on ExternalApi.

class MyService {

    private final ExternalApi externalApi;

    public MyService(ExternalApi externalApi) {
        this.externalApi = externalApi;
    }

    public String fetchData() {
        return externalApi.getData();
    }

    public String fetchDataById(int id) {
        return externalApi.getDataById(id);
    }
}
Explanation
Uses Constructor Injection.
Calls methods of ExternalApi.
Business logic is tested using mocked objects.
3. Unit Test Class

The MyServiceTest class tests MyService using Mockito.

Test Case 1: Mocking a Method
@Test
public void testFetchData_WithMockedApi() {

    ExternalApi mockApi = Mockito.mock(ExternalApi.class);

    when(mockApi.getData()).thenReturn("Mock Data");

    MyService service = new MyService(mockApi);

    String result = service.fetchData();

    assertEquals("Mock Data", result);

}
Explanation
Creates a mock object.
Defines return value using when().thenReturn().
Calls the service method.
Verifies the returned result using assertEquals().
Test Case 2: Parameterized Stubbing
@Test
public void testFetchDataById_WithParameterizedStubbing() {

    ExternalApi mockApi = mock(ExternalApi.class);

    when(mockApi.getDataById(1))
            .thenReturn("User: Alice");

    when(mockApi.getDataById(2))
            .thenReturn("User: Bob");

    MyService service = new MyService(mockApi);

    assertEquals("User: Alice",
            service.fetchDataById(1));

    assertEquals("User: Bob",
            service.fetchDataById(2));

}
Explanation
Returns different values for different input parameters.
Demonstrates parameter-based stubbing.
Ensures correct output for each input.
Test Case 3: Verify Method Call
@Test
public void testFetchData_VerifyInteraction() {

    ExternalApi mockApi = mock(ExternalApi.class);

    when(mockApi.getData())
            .thenReturn("Verified Data");

    MyService service = new MyService(mockApi);

    service.fetchData();

    verify(mockApi, times(1)).getData();

}
Explanation
Calls the service method.
Uses verify() to ensure getData() was called.
times(1) confirms the method executed exactly once.
Mockito Execution Flow
Create Mock Object
        │
        ▼
Stub Method using when()
        │
        ▼
Create Service Object
        │
        ▼
Call Service Method
        │
        ▼
Mock Returns Dummy Data
        │
        ▼
Verify Output using assertEquals()
        │
        ▼
Verify Interaction using verify()
Maven Dependencies

Add the following dependencies to pom.xml.

JUnit 5
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.junit.jupiter</groupId>
    <artifactId>junit-jupiter</artifactId>
    <version>5.10.0</version>
    <scope>test</scope>
</dependency>

Purpose: Provides annotations and assertions for unit testing.

Mockito
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.mockito</groupId>
    <artifactId>mockito-core</artifactId>
    <version>5.8.0</version>
    <scope>test</scope>
</dependency>

Purpose: Creates mock objects and verifies interactions.

Testing Process
JUnit Test
     │
     ▼
Mockito creates Mock Object
     │
     ▼
Stub Required Methods
     │
     ▼
Inject Mock into Service
     │
     ▼
Execute Service Method
     │
     ▼
Compare Expected Output
     │
     ▼
Verify Method Calls
